00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.850
- So how about as a kid,
were you entrepreneurial?

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:28.610
- Yeah, so I grew up in Missouri

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.760
and then I went to college in Tennessee.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.360
And when I was in Tennessee,

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.510
I owned a chain of hot dog stands called

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:36.932
Southern Sam's: Weiner's
as Big as a Baby's Arm.

00:01:36.932 --> 00:01:39.270
(laughing)

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.402
- How old were you?

00:01:40.402 --> 00:01:42.090
- I started when I was like 20.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.060
But before that, I was
selling stuff on Ebay.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.820
But that was my first legal business,

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.330
where I got a business
license and paid taxes,

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.310
and things like that.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.410
Have you seen that TV show
called "American Pickers"?

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:52.243
- Yes.

00:01:52.243 --> 00:01:53.730
- So Mike, the main guy, the skinny guy.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.840
I met him on the street,
'cause I was a big fan.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.250
And I asked him to work at his store,

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.590
he was opening up a store where
they sell all the old shit.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.650
And I worked there, and it was great,

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.220
but there was always a
line of a thousand people.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.397
And I was like, "I'm gonna
go open up a hot dog stand

00:02:08.397 --> 00:02:09.820
"and sell hot dogs to these people."

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:11.370
And that's what happened.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.190
- Because the show was
so famous that people--

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.963
- Yeah when I worked there in 2011,

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.500
or no, sorry, 2008 or nine
or something like that,

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.311
we were number two on
cable, behind "Pawn Stars."

00:02:21.311 --> 00:02:23.550
And all these people from around the world

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.460
would come and get in this line.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:26.293
- Where was that?

00:02:26.293 --> 00:02:27.363
- It was in Nashville.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.550
He's into old stuff, right?

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.250
So he got this old building
that was away from everything

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.110
and there's no restaurants.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.190
And I was like, "Huh."

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.410
I from the south so I can say this,

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:37.870
but they're kind of
rednecks who would come

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.900
and wait in line and I was like,

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.440
these fuckers want some
hot dogs and water,

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:42.300
that's all they want.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.320
And I opened up this hotdog stand

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.777
and that was like my first--

00:02:45.777 --> 00:02:47.653
- Hustle, official.
- Yeah, first business

00:02:47.653 --> 00:02:50.610
that made money and I paid
taxes and got licenses.

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:51.850
- And how did that go?

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.310
How long did you do it?

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.143
- For a few years,

00:02:54.143 --> 00:02:56.150
I mean you would make a
grand a day on a good day.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:56.983
Yeah, it was awesome

00:02:56.983 --> 00:03:01.360
and then I started a website
that made a little bit of money

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.937
but I was like oh the
Internet's the way to go

00:03:02.937 --> 00:03:05.040
and so I left school and moved up

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.040
to Silicon Valley in San Francisco

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.300
and originally had job offers at Airbnb

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.370
